{%- comment -%}
  zv-addon-riders (2026-10-27): resolves zv_addon_rider_by_lead ('lead-handle:rider-handle|...',
  from pricing.config.json addonNames[].ridesWith) into 'leadVariantId:riderVariantId:riderCents|...'.
  Today that is one pair: ADC-750 (koop-video-deurbel-750, the bought Videodeurbel) leads the camera
  subscription: one subscription line at quantity 1 whenever the cart holds an ADC-750 line,
  none otherwise. riderCents is the rider's live product price, never a config amount.

  A pair whose lead or rider product doesn't resolve is left out, so nothing is ever synced
  against a half-known pair. Resolved by handle, never a hardcoded variant id.

  Params: map - zv_addon_rider_by_lead (render scope can't see the caller's variables).
  Usage: capture it, then `| strip | split: '|'`, and split each entry on ':'.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign ar_pairs = map | split: '|'
  assign ar_out = ''
  for kv in ar_pairs
    assign ar_kvp = kv | split: ':'
    assign ar_lead = all_products[ar_kvp[0]].variants.first
    assign ar_rider = all_products[ar_kvp[1]].variants.first
    if ar_lead.id != blank and ar_rider.id != blank
      assign ar_entry = ar_lead.id | append: ':' | append: ar_rider.id | append: ':' | append: ar_rider.price
      if ar_out == ''
        assign ar_out = ar_entry
      else
        assign ar_out = ar_out | append: '|' | append: ar_entry
      endif
    endif
  endfor
  echo ar_out
-%}
